---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site';

const title = "Social Media Management Services | SKYON IT SOLUTIONS";
const description = "We offer social media management services including content planning, creative direction, publishing, and ongoing management.";
const currentUrl = `${SITE.url}/services/social-media`;

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": SITE.url },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Services", "item": `${SITE.url}/#services` },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Social Media Management", "item": currentUrl }
  ]
};

const serviceSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Social Media Management",
  "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "SKYON IT SOLUTIONS", "url": SITE.url },
  "url": currentUrl,
  "description": description
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(serviceSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  
  <article class="pt-32 pb-24 px-4 md:px-8 max-w-[48rem] mx-auto">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-8 text-sm text-text-disabled">
      <ol class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-hover transition-colors">Home</a></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">/</span></li>
        <li><a href="/#services" class="hover:text-brand-hover transition-colors">Services</a></li>
        <li><span aria-hidden="true">/</span></li>
        <li class="text-text-primary" aria-current="page">Social Media Management</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-text-primary tracking-tight mb-8">Social Media Management</h1>
    
    <div class="text-text-body space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Maintaining an active presence on social platforms requires consistent content generation and strategic oversight. We provide social media management services structured around content planning, creative direction, and operational execution.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary mt-12 mb-4">The Role of Social Media</h2>
      <p>
        A social media presence acts as a direct communication channel between a brand and its audience. Effective management of these channels involves more than just posting updates; it requires a structured approach to ensure that the content aligns with broader business objectives and maintains a consistent brand voice across various networks. 
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary mt-12 mb-4">What We Do</h2>
      <p>
        Our social media services focus on these key operational areas:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Content Planning:</strong> We outline content themes and schedules aligned with your brand guidelines.</li>
        <li><strong>Creative Direction:</strong> We coordinate the visual style and messaging approach for your social media assets.</li>
        <li><strong>Publishing:</strong> We handle the scheduling and deployment of posts across selected social media platforms.</li>
        <li><strong>Management:</strong> We keep the content plan and publishing on track.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These activities form a continuous cycle. Content planning sets the structural roadmap by determining the topics and frequency of communication. Creative direction translates that roadmap into tangible assets, dictating how the content will look and sound to ensure brand consistency. Finally, the publishing and management phases handle the actual distribution, scheduling, and organizational oversight required to keep the profiles active.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary mt-12 mb-4">Our Process</h2>
      <p>
        Our approach to social media is organized into the following workflow:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Understand:</strong> We learn about the business and goals.</li>
        <li><strong>Strategize:</strong> We plan the approach.</li>
        <li><strong>Build:</strong> We prepare the content plan and publishing schedule.</li>
        <li><strong>Launch:</strong> We launch the social media presence.</li>
        <li><strong>Grow:</strong> We review how the content is working and adjust the plan.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary mt-12 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <details class="group border-b border-hairline py-4">
        <summary class="font-bold cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-primary text-text-primary">What is the difference between content planning and creative direction?</summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base">Content planning is the organizational process of deciding what topics will be covered and when they will be published. Creative direction involves deciding the aesthetic, tone, and visual elements that will be used to present those topics to the audience.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group border-b border-hairline py-4">
        <summary class="font-bold cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-primary text-text-primary">Why is a publishing schedule important?</summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base">A publishing schedule ensures that content is distributed consistently over time, rather than sporadically.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="group border-b border-hairline py-4">
        <summary class="font-bold cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-primary text-text-primary">How do brand guidelines influence social media?</summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base">Brand guidelines provide the foundational rules for how a business presents itself visually and textually. Adhering to these guidelines on social media ensures that all posts remain recognizable and consistent with the organization's broader identity.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">Ready to discuss your project?</h3>
      <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-button-fill text-[#0A1A05] px-8 py-3 rounded-full font-semibold hover:bg-button-hover transition-colors shadow-sm">
        Contact Us
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-hairline flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-medium">
      <span class="text-text-disabled">Other Services:</span>
      <a href="/services/website-development" class="text-brand-primary hover:text-brand-hover">Website Development</a>
      <a href="/services/seo" class="text-brand-primary hover:text-brand-hover">Search Engine Optimization</a>
      <a href="/services/digital-marketing" class="text-brand-primary hover:text-brand-hover">Digital Marketing</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
